## 1. Direct Recommendation

Replace the noisy dual `↓/↑` badge with a **read-only 3-coin DaisyUI `rating`** where the number of filled coins (and their color: green → amber → red) represents the approximated cost of a **"standard request" (1K input + 1K output tokens)**. Combine it with a compact `~$x.xx` / `~x cxj` estimate. This gives an instant "Fable is pricier than Haiku/DeepSeek" signal without parsing raw token tables.

---

## 2. Specifications

| Dimension | Decision |
|---|---|
| **Cost basis** | `cost = input_per_1k × 1 + output_per_1k × 1` (standard request = 1K in + 1K out). Constant `STANDARD_REQUEST` at module scope. |
| **Tiering** | Relative bucket across the loaded model set: `ratio ≤ 0.33 → cheap`, `≤ 0.66 → moderate`, `else → expensive`. |
| **Coin encoding** | `cheap → 1 coin`, `moderate → 2`, `expensive → 3`. Filled coins take the tier color; empty coins are `text-base-content/15`. |
| **Colors** | `cheap → text-success`, `moderate → text-warning`, `expensive → text-error` (semantic, WCAG-safe pairings). |
| **Card layout** | Row 1: icon · name + provider/model subtitle · selection check. Row 2 (hairline `border-t`): coin rating · cost estimate. |
| **Card states** | Default: `bg-base-100 border-base-300`; Hover: `hover:bg-base-200 hover:border-base-content/20`; Selected: `bg-primary/15 border-primary/50 ring-1 ring-primary/40`. |
| **Typography** | Name `text-xs font-semibold`, subtitle/cost `text-[10px]`, all `truncate` + `min-w-0` to survive grid squeeze. |
| **Radius / motion** | `rounded-xl`, `transition-all duration-150`. |
| **Currency** | Model-level = `cxj`, provider `price_list` = `$`; label reflects whichever source resolved. |

---

## 3. Code

```vue src/components/chat/ChatLLMModelSelector.vue
